{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-p44q-fmwr-jqr7","published":"2026-06-24T15:31:47Z","modified":"2026-09-25T19:15:04.533348168Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-57297"],"summary":"Jenkins Contrast Continuous Application Security Plugin has a missing permission check","details":"Jenkins Contrast Continuous Application Security Plugin 3.11 and earlier does not perform a permission check in an HTTP endpoint that tests the connection to a Contrast TeamServer.\n\nThis allows attackers with Overall/Read permission to connect to an attacker-specified URL using an attacker-specified username, API key, and service key.\n\nAdditionally, this HTTP endpoint does not require POST requests, resulting in a cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability.\n\nContrast Continuous Application Security Plugin 3.12 requires Overall/Administer permission and POST requests to test the connection to a Contrast TeamServer.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.jenkins-ci.plugins:contrast-continuous-application-security","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.jenkins-ci.plugins/contrast-continuous-application-security"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.12"}]}],"versions":["1.0","1.1","1.2","1.3","1.4","1.6","2.0","2.1","2.10","2.10-beta","2.10-beta2","2.11","2.12","2.12.1","2.2","2.3","2.4","2.5","2.6","2.7","2.8","2.8-beta","2.9","3.0","3.0.1","3.1","3.1.1","3.10","3.11","3.2","3.3","3.4","3.5","3.6","3.7","3.8.1","3.8.2","3.8.3","3.9"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/06/GHSA-p44q-fmwr-jqr7/GHSA-p44q-fmwr-jqr7.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-57297"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/jenkinsci/contrast-continuous-application-security-plugin/commit/ddea0a815aec52c0695d8c0c7f09f9cfce4989e5"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/jenkinsci/contrast-continuous-application-security-plugin"},{"type":"WEB","url":"